e four braids that are  left out in this style  i would  then attach the  pre-braided jimbei headpiece  i would take  some hair thread and a curved needle and  i gently sew  the hair piece to the surrounding braids  to make sure that it is sturdy and  centered so that it's not adding any  additional stress onto the model's head  because it is heavy  now that i have attached my gym bay  piece which is the center piece of this  hairstyle i must do some finishing steps  i'm going to come through with a  setting foam it kind of sets that style  into your hair  i usually add a silk scarf to lay the  design down so that it dries in that  position  [Music]  once i feel that the braids are  sufficiently dry and set i will remove  the scarf  and reveal  the beautiful braid pattern beneath my  goodness  like i can't believe that this is  my head  like i feel like  a queen  the whole time that i'm braiding i'm  thinking  um damn i'm messing uh damn it's not  gonna come out right oh wow this isn't  gonna come out right  but then once i can see all of the  effort totally finished it's the finish  line that you've seen in your mind but  now it has been made manifest  and you can  see what you put into it and you can  just bask in the glory of the beauty you  created  [Music]  black people oftentimes refer to  their hair as their crown  if you ask you know western society  where's your soul people point to their  chest right it's in here but across a  lot of west africa you point to the head  as the space where the soul rests  it's the top it's the closest thing to  the divine that we get on this side of  heaven  the resurgence of braids among black  people for me has been great i'm glad to  see black people be able to love  themselves and to love the beauty in  their natural appearance  it's something that i received as a  child something that has given me a  vision to want to promote that and it's  something that i hope my work promotes  that we are stronger together and that  t